{"kind":"assert","text":"Source review for bearer retry repair5d41ea36: the intended grantor-key rule is already stated in R-CRED-3 (protocol.md:570): revoking the member's key ends the bearer session. R-CRED-10 should name that case explicitly. At exact e6, requests.ts authenticateHash:167 rejects a revoked delegation grantor; judgeBearer:334–344 omits it. Align token validity before constructing an envelope, including exact bearer retries. Preserve R-IDEM-2: a caller-retained signed envelope remains replayable after key revocation; admission.ts:290–301 returns matching stored results before current act authority. Do not move per-kind/role/lane/binding admission checks ahead of a valid token's exact retry.\n\nA decisive bounded witness should retire the grantor key, rather than only compromise it: admission.ts:1431–1432 already cascades compromised revocation into delegation revocation and can mask the missing grantor check. Admit/retain one act, retire its grantor, assert reads and bearer exact retry are unauthenticated, and directly replay the retained signed bytes to assert the original result and no new entry. One hand-made distinguishing omission/control suffices; no sweep.\n\nAdjacent source mismatch to resolve explicitly within alignment or track as a separate named decision: authenticateHash:169–170 rejects an inactive/removed session member; judgeBearer ignores member state; roster remove in admission.ts:1424–1425 marks the member removed without revoking the delegation. This supports an exact-retry authentication concern, not an independently executed counterexample here. Member removal must not be accidentally conflated with role changes: current reads do not invalidate a token merely because role/kind permissions changed; new admissions still judge those restrictions. Keep bearer-only lookup and held signing-key requirements when sharing validity logic.\n\nRoot read the quoted protocol/source boundaries and a parallel source-only review. No canonical edit, installation, runtime test or provider operation was performed. This is guidance for the existing tracked repair, not source approval or a new protocol adoption.","body":{"scope":"source-only rule and repair-boundary review; no runtime verdict","source_head":"e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967"}}